snowplow-identities 0.2.0 (2026-YY-ZZ)
---------------------------------------
See MIGRATION.md for upgrade steps and rebuild recipes for the removed tables.

Breaking changes
- `snowplow_identities_id_changes` removed.
- `snowplow_identities_id_mapping_scd` removed.
- `snowplow_identities_new_identities` renamed to `snowplow_identities_identities`, and its
  per-identifier columns removed. Those values live in
  `snowplow_identities_identifier_mapping` at the identifier grain.
- `snowplow_identities_snowplow_id_mapping` and `snowplow_identities_merge_events` gain a
  `load_tstamp` column and are now partitioned on it. Drop both before the first run.
- `snowplow__allow_refresh`, `snowplow__dev_target_name` and the `models_to_remove` var are
  removed with the manifest. `--full-refresh` now rebuilds from `snowplow__start_date`.

Changed
- `snowplow_identities_identifier_mapping` is now a view over the new
  `snowplow_identities_identifier_mapping_base` table, resolved to the current
  `active_snowplow_id` at read time. Columns, grain and values are unchanged.
- Each model tracks its own progress off its own `max(load_tstamp)` instead of a shared
  manifest, retiring the manifest, the base layer, the `_this_run` scratch layer and every
  run hook. 15 models become 5 plus a view, and every dependency is a real `ref()`.
- Every model except `snowplow_identities_stg_identity_events` extends its window's upper
  bound to that model's watermark when its own is behind, so a sparse event stream cannot
  strand a model.
- `snowplow_identities_stg_identity_events` replaces whole days instead of matching every
  `event_id`. BigQuery uses `insert_overwrite` with `copy_partitions`, Snowflake uses
  `delete+insert` keyed on the load date. The window is day-aligned, so this is equivalent to
  the upsert and takes the per-event key matching out of every run.

Added
- Run-window logging, replacing the manifest framework's `print_run_limits`.
- `snowplow__lookback_days` (default 1), the overlap re-scanned each run for late-arriving
  data.
- `snowplow__partition_tstamp`, `snowplow__partition_tstamp_type` and
  `snowplow__partition_buffer_days`, for when `atomic.events` is partitioned on something
  other than `load_tstamp`.
- `snowplow_identities_identifier_mapping` gains `mapping_state` and `is_preferred`.
  `mapping_state` says how many identities an identifier resolves to, and whether they can
  be put in age order. `is_preferred` marks the row to use when you want one row per
  identifier.
- `snowplow__merge_limit_collapse` (default false). It lets `is_preferred` pick the identity
  holding an identifier's most recent sighting when the identifier has several. Only safe
  when no identifier is configured as unique in the identity service.

Fixed
- Merges no longer rewrite, re-point or delete identifier rows.
  `snowplow_identities_identifier_mapping_base` is keyed on an immutable surrogate of
  (snowplow_id, id_type, id_value).
- An identifier that later reappears under a new identity keeps both rows rather than
  overwriting the first.
- Keys untouched for longer than `snowplow__upsert_lookback_days` no longer duplicate on
  upsert. `snowplow_optimize` is off on `identities`, `identifier_mapping_base` and
  `snowplow_id_mapping`.
- `identity_merge` events are filtered to the `snowplow-identities` app_id rather than
  `snowplow__app_id`, which dropped every merge event when set.

Removed
- The `snowplow_identities_snowplow_id_mapping_affected` pre-hook snapshot table and the
  `snowplow_identities_internal` source that read it.
- The `delete_stale_identifier_mapping_rows` macro and its post-hook.

